MARGINAL REVENUE-MARGINAL COST APPROACH
(MR-MC APPROACH).J
Both the conditions are needed for Producer's Equilibrium
MC = MR
We know, MR is the addition to TR from sale of
one more unit of output and MC is addition to TС
for increasing production by one unit. Every
producer aims to maximize the total profits. For
this, a firm compares its MR with its MC. Profits
will increase as long as MR exceeds MC and
profits will fall if MR is lessthan MC. So,
equilibrium is not achieved when MC = MR as it is
possible to add to profits by producing more.
Producer is also not in equilibrium when MC > MR
because benefit is less than the cost. It means,
the firm will be at equilibrium when MC = MR.
