MC = MR is a necessary condition, but not
sufficient enough to ensure equilibrium. It is
because MC = MR may occur at more than one
level of output. However, out of these, only that
output level is the equilibrium output when MC
becomes greater than MR after the equilibrium.
It is because if MC is greater than MR, then
producing beyond MC = MR output will reduce
profits. On the other hand, if MC is less than MR
beyond MC = MR output, it is possible to add to
profits by producing more. So, first condition
must be supplemented with the second
condition to attain the producer's equilibrium.
